        "prefix_token_count": 67,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: To find the value of \\(d\\), we can use the properties of the sine function and its periodicity. We know that \\(\\sin(x)\\) is an odd function, meaning \\(\\sin(-x) = -\\sin(x)\\). This property will help us determine the coefficients in the given equation."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 367,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 369,
        "char_start": 260,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 115,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 116,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Substitute \\(x = 0\\) into the equation \\((\\sin x)^7 = a \\sin 7x + b \\sin 5x + c \\sin 3x + d \\sin x\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 761,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 763,
        "char_start": 371,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 297,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 298,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: When \\(x = 0\\), \\(\\sin(0) = 0\\), so \\((\\sin 0)^7 = 0^7 = 0\\). Also, \\(\\sin(7 \\cdot 0) = \\sin(0) = 0\\), \\(\\sin(5 \\cdot 0) = \\sin(0) = 0\\), \\(\\sin(3 \\cdot 0) = \\sin(0) = 0\\), and \\(\\sin(0) = 0\\). Therefore, the equation simplifies to:\n\\[0 = a \\cdot 0 + b \\cdot 0 + c \\cdot 0 + d \\cdot 0.\\]\nThis does not provide information about \\(d\\) directly since it equals 0 for any \\(a, b, c, d\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1326,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1327,
        "char_start": 765,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 548,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 549,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Substitute \\(x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) into the equation. Note that \\(\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\), so \\((\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{2})^7 = 1^7 = 1\\). Also, \\(\\sin\\left(7 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{2}\\right) = -1\\), \\(\\sin\\left(5 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\), \\(\\sin\\left(3 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right) = -1\\), and \\(\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\). Therefore, the equation becomes:\n\\[1 = a(-1) + b(1) + c(-1) + d(1).\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[1 = -a + b - c + d.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1906,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1907,
        "char_start": 1329,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 810,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 811,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Substitute \\(x = -\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) into the equation. Note that \\(\\sin\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = -1\\), so \\((\\sin -\\frac{\\pi}{2})^7 = (-1)^7 = -1\\). Also, \\(\\sin\\left(7 \\cdot -\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(-\\frac{7\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\), \\(\\sin\\left(5 \\cdot -\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(-\\frac{5\\pi}{2}\\right) = -1\\), \\(\\sin\\left(3 \\cdot -\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(-\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\), and \\(\\sin\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = -1\\). Therefore, the equation becomes:\n\\[-1 = a(1) + b(-1) + c(1) + d(-1).\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[-1 = a - b + c - d.\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2170,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2172,
        "char_start": 1909,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 916,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 917,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Add the two equations obtained from substituting \\(x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) and \\(x = -\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\):\n\\[1 = -a + b - c + d,\\]\n\\[-1 = a - b + c - d.\\]\nAdding these equations gives:\n\\[0 = 0 + 0 + 0 + 2d,\\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[0 = 2d.\\]\nTherefore, \\(d = 0\\)."
      }
