  "raw_text": "Step 1: To find the value of \\(d\\), we can use the properties of the sine function and its periodicity. We know that \\(\\sin(x)\\) is an odd function, meaning \\(\\sin(-x) = -\\sin(x)\\). This property will help us determine the coefficients in the given equation.\n\nStep 2: Substitute \\(x = 0\\) into the equation \\((\\sin x)^7 = a \\sin 7x + b \\sin 5x + c \\sin 3x + d \\sin x\\).\n\nStep 3: When \\(x = 0\\), \\(\\sin(0) = 0\\), so \\((\\sin 0)^7 = 0^7 = 0\\). Also, \\(\\sin(7 \\cdot 0) = \\sin(0) = 0\\), \\(\\sin(5 \\cdot 0) = \\sin(0) = 0\\), \\(\\sin(3 \\cdot 0) = \\sin(0) = 0\\), and \\(\\sin(0) = 0\\). Therefore, the equation simplifies to:\n\\[0 = a \\cdot 0 + b \\cdot 0 + c \\cdot 0 + d \\cdot 0.\\]\nThis does not provide information about \\(d\\) directly since it equals 0 for any \\(a, b, c, d\\).\n\nStep 4: Substitute \\(x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) into the equation. Note that \\(\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\), so \\((\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{2})^7 = 1^7 = 1\\). Also, \\(\\sin\\left(7 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{2}\\right) = -1\\), \\(\\sin\\left(5 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\), \\(\\sin\\left(3 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right) = -1\\), and \\(\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\). Therefore, the equation becomes:\n\\[1 = a(-1) + b(1) + c(-1) + d(1).\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[1 = -a + b - c + d.\\]\n\nStep 5: Substitute \\(x = -\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) into the equation. Note that \\(\\sin\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = -1\\), so \\((\\sin -\\frac{\\pi}{2})^7 = (-1)^7 = -1\\). Also, \\(\\sin\\left(7 \\cdot -\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(-\\frac{7\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\), \\(\\sin\\left(5 \\cdot -\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(-\\frac{5\\pi}{2}\\right) = -1\\), \\(\\sin\\left(3 \\cdot -\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(-\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\), and \\(\\sin\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = -1\\). Therefore, the equation becomes:\n\\[-1 = a(1) + b(-1) + c(1) + d(-1).\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[-1 = a - b + c - d.\\]\n\nStep 6: Add the two equations obtained from substituting \\(x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) and \\(x = -\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\):\n\\[1 = -a + b - c + d,\\]\n\\[-1 = a - b + c - d.\\]\nAdding these equations gives:\n\\[0 = 0 + 0 + 0 + 2d,\\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[0 = 2d.\\]\nTherefore, \\(d = 0\\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{0}<|im_end|>",
